@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title ACCEPTED — GitHub access during proveo init
' Implemented contract: _spec/cmd/proveo/github-access.puml
' Existing flow: _spec/cmd/proveo/github-credentials.puml
' Existing pages: _spec/cmd/proveo/init-sbx-bootstrap.puml
' Existing host keys: _spec/packages/lib/github-ssh-hosts.puml
'
' EVIDENCE, read 2026-11-08:
' https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/configuration/credentials/#ssh-agent
' https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/configuration/settings/#sshagentforwardingenabled
' https://github.com/docker/sbx-releases/issues/835
' https://github.com/docker/sbx-kits-contrib/tree/main/github-ssh
' https://cli.github.com/manual/gh_auth_login
'
' CURRENT SOURCE:
' cmd/proveo/init_tui.go offers gh now/later on setup page 1 of 3.
' cmd/proveo/init_github.go stores the API token under sbx service github.
' internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go builds capabilities from vendored kits
' and adds credentials, network policy and lifecycle; it adds no ssh-agent@1.
' internal/sbx/third_party/{claude,codex,cursor,opencode}.yaml request no
' ssh-agent@1 capability.
' packages/lib/hooks/git-sync-turn.sh uses command-local HTTPS for GitHub
' SSH remotes, regardless of the host's gh transport preference.
'
' ACCEPTED POLICY:
' Offer the host's github.com Git protocol as the initial selection.
' The operator explicitly accepts sandbox SSH access before it is enabled.
' Keep API authentication independent of Git transport.
' Treat trust repo as a separate capability throughout this proposal.

rectangle "Setup page 1/3\nGitHub: now / later" as SETUP
rectangle "GitHub access\ncontextual panel during the existing gh stage" as PANEL
rectangle "SSH agent\nforward host agent" as SSH
rectangle "HTTPS token\nsbx github service" as HTTPS
rectangle "Later\nGit access deferred" as LATER
rectangle "Host configured\nsandbox verification pending" as HOST
rectangle "Sandbox authentication verified\nrepository permissions checked separately" as VERIFIED

SETUP --> PANEL : now
PANEL --> SSH
PANEL --> HTTPS
PANEL --> LATER
SSH --> HOST
HTTPS --> HOST
HOST --> VERIFIED : probe actual workload configuration

note right of PANEL
  Proposed panel; values below are examples.
  GitHub API       signed in as <login>
  Host Git         SSH
  Sandbox Git      [SSH agent] HTTPS token later
  Host SSH agent   reachable; <n> keys
end note

note bottom of SSH
  Show exposed key fingerprints.
  Keep private keys on the host.
  Forwarding allows use of exposed keys.
  Never imply one selected fingerprint
  restricts an agent exposing more keys.
end note

note bottom of HTTPS
  Use sbx's github service for API + Git.
  Preserve host gh preference and remotes.
  Apply transport adaptation inside sbx.
  Run and Stop hook use the same policy.
end note

note bottom of HOST
  Check the effective socket and host keys.
  Inspect forwarding + runtime capability.
  Report repairs before applying changes.
  Missing key: guide loading/registration.
  Recovery: retry / HTTPS / later.
end note

note bottom of VERIFIED
  Check a real socket and ssh-add inside sbx.
  Verify SSH identity with GitHub's greeting.
  GitHub ssh -T exits 1 on success.
  Keep API and SSH identities distinct.
  Read access never proves push permission.
end note

' APPLY AND VERIFY:
' API sign-in remains useful for gh commands when Git uses SSH. Missing API
' credentials must not be reported as missing SSH authentication, or vice versa.
' Keep existing gh preferences; let gh own login and explicit key-upload flows.
' Use the configured sbx agent socket, or the invoking client's SSH_AUTH_SOCK.
' Do not pin a transient socket as a permanent host setting by default.
' Do not silently enable host-wide forwarding or restart a running daemon.
' Show the scope and restart requirement in the repair action the user accepts.
' SSH requires com.docker.sandbox/ssh-agent@1 for phase runtime in the actual
' v3 workload; known_hosts alone cannot provide authentication.
' Capability changes require a newly created workload; do not promise a restart
' adds a missing capability to an existing locked v3 sandbox.
' Verify using the effective workload, agent and network policy. If init cannot
' perform that probe, show verification pending and check before agent handoff
' in proveo run. A generic host-only probe must never mark a workload verified.
' Where a repository is available, verify its effective push destination with
' read-only checks; label write access unverified until a real authorized push.
' Init creates no test commit or remote ref. Outside a repository, defer its
' access check to proveo run. Distinguish branch-policy rejection from auth.
' Preserve host SSH aliases and explicit push URLs when resolving the target;
' unsupported host/alias configuration needs a specific diagnostic.
' On --yes/non-TTY, provision existing API credentials as today, report SSH
' readiness, and do not introduce a new forwarding grant or interactive repair.
' Future runs and the Stop hook must consume the persisted selected transport.
' An SSH failure offers a visible HTTPS choice, never a silent fallback.
'
' ALTERNATIVES surfaced to Executor:
' 1. Follow host transport (recommended).
' 2. Always use HTTPS inside sbx while preserving host SSH configuration.
' 3. Guide a dedicated automation key + host agent instead of the regular agent.
' A dedicated public key belongs at GitHub; its private key stays with that
' host agent. A public key stored as an sbx secret cannot authenticate.
@enduml
